{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"planarLayout","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Drawing","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Drawing","preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"text":">?","kind":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Return Value","anchor":"return-value"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The drawing, in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order, or nil when the graph has no planar embedding."}]}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The drawing comes from ","type":"text"},{"code":"planarEmbedding()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" by de Fraysseix, Pach and Pollack’s shift method","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in Chrobak and Payne’s linear-time form. The embedding of the underlying simple graph","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(self-loops and parallel copies drawn as one segment) is first made connected, by an edge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from the first vertex of each component to the first vertex of the next, and every face","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"boundary a simple cycle; then every face but the largest (the outer face) is triangulated.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The vertices are placed in a canonical ordering of that graph, each one above the contour","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of those before it, the contour shifted to make room. The added edges are not drawn and not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reported. Every vertex has integer coordinates with 0 ≤ x ≤ 2n − 4 and 0 ≤ y ≤ n − 2, and no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"two edges cross or overlap. Fewer than four vertices are placed at (0, 0), (2, 0) and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(1, 1) in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order. The drawing is not rescaled (","type":"text"},{"code":"rescaled(scale:center:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" maps it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to a common frame). A directed graph is drawn through ","type":"text"},{"code":"undirectedView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"de Fraysseix, Pach and Pollack, “How to draw a planar graph on a grid”, Combinatorica"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"10(1), 1990."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Chrobak and Payne, “A linear-time algorithm for drawing a planar graph on a grid”,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Information Processing Letters 54(4), 1995."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"O(n + m) for the embedding, then O(n) expected (hashing the triangulation’s vertex pairs).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"As for ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"planarEmbedding()"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","name":"Precondition","style":"note"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/planarLayout()"},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/graphprotocols\/graph\/planarlayout()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing","doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"metadata":{"role":"symbol","title":"planarLayout()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"planarLayout","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Drawing","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"text":">?","kind":"text"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"PlanarLayout.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphDrawing\/PlanarLayout.swift#L31"},"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P0A7DrawingE12planarLayoutAD0C0Vy6VertexQzGSgyF","modules":[{"name":"GraphDrawing","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"roleHeading":"Instance Method","symbolKind":"method","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols"},"abstract":[{"text":"A crossing-free straight-line drawing on an integer grid, or nil when the graph is not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"planar.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph/Vertex":{"abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph\/vertex","title":"Vertex","fragments":[{"text":"associatedtype","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://GraphDrawing/documentation/GraphDrawing":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing","title":"GraphDrawing","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphdrawing","role":"collection","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://GraphDrawing/documentation/GraphDrawing/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/graphprotocols\/graph","type":"topic","title":"Graph","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"extension"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","text":"Graph"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://GraphDrawing/documentation/GraphDrawing/GraphProtocols/Graph/planarLayout()":{"title":"planarLayout()","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"planarLayout","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Drawing","preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">?","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/planarLayout()","url":"\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/graphprotocols\/graph\/planarlayout()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A crossing-free straight-line drawing on an integer grid, or nil when the graph is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"planar."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://GraphDrawing/documentation/GraphDrawing/Drawing":{"title":"Drawing","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Drawing"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Drawing","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A position in the plane for each vertex, in a fixed vertex order: what every layout in this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"module returns, and what a caller passes as a starting drawing."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/drawing","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Drawing"}]},"doc://GraphDrawing/documentation/GraphDrawing/GraphProtocols":{"abstract":[],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/graphprotocols","title":"GraphProtocols","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols","role":"collection","kind":"symbol"}}}